1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:27,420
I promise.

3
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:29,820
As long as you let me stay on the School Team,

4
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,190
I'm even willing to do chores.

5
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,150
I'll think about it.

6
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:35,100
Tomorrow night, dinner's on me!

7
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:37,980
How about we all have a big, fancy feast?

8
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:39,900
Yeah!

9
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:43,260
The thing I've been dreaming about has finally come true!

10
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:45,150
Mini, I've put together a set of moves

11
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:46,620
specifically to counter your Light Wheel technique.

12
00:01:47,430 --> 00:01:48,270
Really?

13
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:49,500
Captain!

14
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:52,860
Looks like Leo's trying to stage a comeback.

15
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:56,670
Our Team has a schedule for where and when we train,

16
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:57,660
and it's all planned out.

17
00:01:58,300 --> 00:01:59,580
Why do you have to mess up my whole plan?

18
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:01,520
Don't use your plan as an excuse to push me around.

19
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:04,860
There's absolutely no way Jianghai Team
is giving up this platform.

20
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Episode 17

21
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:13,500
I don't want your theories.

22
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:14,940
All I want is Leo's advice.

23
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:17,310
Leo's advice is part of my theories.

24
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:18,780
Advice is advice!

25
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:21,180
Every time you start talking about theories,
my head feels like it's gonna explode.

26
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:25,020
So shallow. So shallow.
You truly lack any real understanding.

27
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:35,100
Look at Leo, acting like he's the Sun or something.

28
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:38,460
And everyone's just circling around
him like a bunch of Planets.

29
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:43,740
What, does he think he's the Captain now?

30
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:47,100
You've really hit the nail on the head there.

31
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:49,500
Whenever Leo's around,

32
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:51,420
nobody listens to a word you say, Captain.

33
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:56,820
This Team just isn't big enough for the both of us.

34
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:59,100
Alright, everyone! Come get your new uniforms!

35
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:18,300
Looking good!

36
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:20,700
Looking sharp. Fits you well.

37
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:24,540
Now that's what a Championship Team looks like.

38
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:26,460
Yeah, exactly.

39
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,340
Hey, where's Chuck?

40
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:30,780
He's still getting dressed.

41
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,660
That guy's always half a step behind everyone else.

42
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:35,070
Coach!

43
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:37,500
I'm done! All set!

44
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:39,910
Coach! I'm ready.

45
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:46,620
Chuck! No way.

46
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:49,020
But I had them made exactly to your measurements.

47
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:51,900
Coach, have you seen how fast Chuck's been growing?

48
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:53,820
Didn't think about that, did you?

49
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:57,660
Chuck, you gotta lose some weight.

50
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:00,060
I can't exactly make you a new Uniform

51
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:01,500
every single month.

52
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:03,390
Right, more like every single week!

53
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:07,310
Coach! I only eat 5 steamed buns a day now.

54
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:23,100
Captain, I have an idea.

55
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:24,990
How about during our break time,

56
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,460
we go check out Jianghai Team's practice?

57
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:28,860
That's actually a pretty good idea.

58
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:30,780
But the Coach would never agree to it.

59
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:32,220
How would she even know?

60
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:33,660
We'd go during break time.

61
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:35,100
She won't be watching us that closely.

62
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:38,460
Right? She's not even here right now.

63
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:39,900
Exactly!

64
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:44,220
The problem is, the second we show up,

65
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:46,140
Jianghai Team will be on guard against us.

66
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:49,980
Captain, I've already got all the props ready for this.

67
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:57,180
Let's go!

68
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:04,860
Looking good.

69
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:12,060
Alright, you head to the sand pit, I'll take the riverbank.

70
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:13,980
Those are the two most likely places

71
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
where they'd be Training.

72
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:17,420
Got it. Let's go!

73
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:36,540
Nobody's here.

74
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:40,860
Captain, it's all up to you now.

75
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:35,100
Why are they still just practicing the basics?

76
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:53,820
Nothing. Not a single thing.

77
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,060
Captain, I have another idea.

78
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Ok.

79
00:07:13,960 --> 00:07:14,940
So, Captain?

80
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:17,340
Still came up completely empty.

81
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:20,700
Let's keep trying.

82
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:49,980
I've used up every single prop I brought with me.

83
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:53,820
Looks like there's just no hope.

84
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,700
I heard their Coach say

85
00:07:57,640 --> 00:07:59,580
that they need to really nail down the basics first,

86
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:04,380
and only once they've built up enough
can they start learning Signature Moves.

87
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:05,500
What?

88
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:08,700
How long is that gonna take?

89
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:12,060
I mean, the Big Tournament's still a ways off anyway.

90
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,420
And what if they go back to school and keep training?

91
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:18,300
Then spying on them is gonna be even harder.

92
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,000
I got it.

93
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,000
Yeah!

94
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:41,340
Captain, you really are one step ahead of the game.

95
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,200
Put it back on.

96
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:56,220
Jacky!

97
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:59,100
How's the Training been feeling for you guys lately?

98
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:00,060
Great!

99
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:01,320
This kind of intense Training

100
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:02,940
has really gotten everyone's feel for the Yo-Yo

101
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:04,860
into peak condition fast.

102
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:07,260
And everyone's much more comfortable

103
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:08,700
with their own Signature Moves now.

104
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:12,540
You need to crank up the intensity for the next phase.

105
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:15,900
After all, Jianghai Team's been training
for half a month longer than us.

106
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:17,820
Don't worry, Coach.

107
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:19,260
We'll definitely make up for the lost time.

108
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:23,550
Coach, I want to keep training like this non-stop.

109
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:25,020
We just need to change things up a bit.

110
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:28,200
I have a suggestion. Let me know what you think.

111
00:09:28,210 --> 00:09:29,370
Yeah, go ahead.

112
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:31,260
I propose we set up an Exhibition Match with Jianghai Team.

113
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:32,700
A Friendly Exhibition Match.

114
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:36,540
This way, we can boost the Team's morale,

115
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,430
and it'll also be a good way to test

116
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:40,350
the results of our Training so far.

117
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:41,340
Hey, that's a great idea!

118
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:44,300
Good.

119
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:46,620
I'll go talk to their Coach Tony about it right now.

120
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:49,500
You guys hurry back and get back to Training!

121
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:58,140
What is it you need now?

122
00:09:58,600 --> 00:10:01,020
Don't tell me you're trying to give

123
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:02,460
that morning Training slot back to us?

124
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:04,860
What, are you this petty?

125
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:07,230
Are you still holding a grudge over that?

126
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:09,150
I'm just kidding. If I were really that petty,

127
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:10,440
I wouldn't have given it to you in the first place.

128
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:13,500
Alright, now that's the Tony I know!

129
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:18,780
What's the point of us always
butting heads like this?

130
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:22,140
I actually do have a pretty great suggestion.

131
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:26,460
Alright then, I'm all ears.

132
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:28,380
Here's what I'm thinking.

133
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:31,740
It's rare that our two teams get to train in the same place.

134
00:10:32,680 --> 00:10:35,100
It's not good for us to just
completely ignore each other, right?

135
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:38,940
So how about we have a Friendly Exhibition Match?

136
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:41,310
One, it could serve as

137
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:42,780
a warm-up for the Fall Yo-Yo Tournament.

138
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:44,700
And two, it'd let us test out

139
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:47,100
how effective each of our Teams' Training has been.

140
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:49,020
So, what do you say?

141
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:51,900
Yeah! That's a really great idea.

142
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:55,230
But I should head back and discuss it with my Team first.

143
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:57,180
Okay. When can you get back to me?

144
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:00,720
How about tomorrow?

145
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:01,580
Sounds good.

146
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:07,740
Awesome!

147
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:09,660
When we've got a goal coming up soon,

148
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:11,100
Training has a lot more drive.

149
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:13,980
We need to pick up the pace of our Training

150
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:15,420
to be ready for this.

151
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:17,340
I've been wanting to speed things up for ages!

152
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:20,220
I'm so sick of practicing these basic moves over and over.

153
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:24,060
I've been wanting to go head-to-head
with Chengnan Team for so long!

154
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:25,980
You're making it sound so violent.

155
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:27,610
Like it's a bloodbath or something.

156
00:11:28,260 --> 00:11:28,860
Mickey.

157
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:31,710
When are you gonna learn to use words correctly?

158
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:33,660
It's called "exaggeration"! Don't you get it?

159
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:34,870
It's just some light humor!

160
00:11:36,220 --> 00:11:37,980
Okay, so that settles it.

161
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:39,710
No one has any objections, right?

162
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:40,980
Wait a minute.

163
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:43,260
I see things a little differently.

164
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,180
I think this Match

165
00:11:45,440 --> 00:11:46,620
is coming at us a little too suddenly.

166
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:49,500
Maybe we should think about it a bit more?

167
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:53,820
What's there to even think about?

168
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:57,660
Hesitating and second-guessing is the
worst thing you can do before a Match.

169
00:11:58,120 --> 00:12:00,990
Coach, Chengnan Team has been
targeting us the whole time.

170
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:01,980
And now out of nowhere, they propose
a Friendly Exhibition Match?

171
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:03,900
That doesn't fit their style at all.

172
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:07,260
There's gotta be a trap. And besides,

173
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:09,660
Shawn, nobody asked you!

174
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:13,020
"Think about it"?

175
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:14,460
That's just a fancy way of putting it.

176
00:12:15,580 --> 00:12:17,790
Aren't you guys being a little too Cowardly?

177
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:18,780
Teddy.

178
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:23,580
Of course.

179
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:27,900
I don't really agree with Leo and
Shawn's take on this either.

180
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:30,300
Saying they're laying a trap for us?

181
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:35,580
I know Coach Sarah very well.

182
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:37,980
She would never do something like that.

183
00:12:41,020 --> 00:12:42,750
You better be fully prepared.

184
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:43,530
Our Jianghai Team

185
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:45,630
Is ready to accept your Challenge!

186
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:49,020
Great! Then we'll just have to see
who comes out on top at the match.

187
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:53,340
Settle it at the match?
Sure, that's fine. But in general,

188
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:55,830
Could you just not try to one-up me all the time?

189
00:12:57,160 --> 00:12:58,590
What do you mean "in general"?

190
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:00,060
When have I ever tried to one-up you?

191
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:03,420
See? There you go again.

192
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:05,340
That tone of yours is exactly what I'm talking about.

193
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:06,780
What's wrong with my tone?

194
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:12,060
Fine. We'll settle this on the field.

195
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:14,460
Bye.

196
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:18,300
Hey! You explain yourself before you walk away!

197
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,960
Shawn, you sure have it easy.

198
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:35,990
Just staring up at the blue sky and white clouds.

199
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:41,340
You're looking at this way too superficially.

200
00:13:41,490 --> 00:13:42,300
What?

201
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:45,630
My brainwaves are firing through
a dense grid of neurons,

202
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:49,980
zipping and racing around like lightning bolts.

203
00:13:50,880 --> 00:13:54,140
Every thinking cell in my body is on high alert,

204
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:57,180
answering the call of inspiration.

205
00:13:57,640 --> 00:13:58,140
Got it?

206
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:00,030
Our Signature Moves can only be practiced

207
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:01,310
late at night when everyone else is asleep.

208
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:04,070
Why?

209
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:06,780
Don't ask. Just do what I tell you.

210
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:13,020
Shawn, I think understanding what you say

211
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:15,900
is even harder than practicing my Signature Moves. Bye!

212
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,260
Jerk.

213
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:25,020
Hey, Captain.

214
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:27,420
We can't go back there again tomorrow.

215
00:15:28,740 --> 00:15:31,260
If we keep going, we're bound to get caught.

216
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,140
It's been enough already.

217
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:37,500
I've got a pretty clear idea now of
what Signature Moves they're working on.

218
00:15:38,620 --> 00:15:40,830
Now it's just up to us to

219
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:42,780
figure out how to deal with them.

220
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:47,100
Besides, we got plenty out of today.

221
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:48,540
It was pretty productive.

222
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:50,460
See?

223
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:52,860
What kind of dumb idea was that?

224
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:55,260
Come on, let's go!

225
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:56,700
Lets hurry up and get back.

226
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,900
I may not have heard the voice of the Earth tonight,

227
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:22,140
but I still got something unexpected out of it. Hmph.

228
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:26,940
No, no. It's not about flicking it with your hand.

229
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:28,380
It's about the Yo-Yo's momentum.

230
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:31,740
When the Yo-Yo comes back, that's when you catch it.

231
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:36,540
I think there's someone there.

232
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:38,940
It's Shawn.

233
00:16:58,120 --> 00:17:00,060
Alright, everyone take a break!

234
00:17:05,320 --> 00:17:06,780
Do you want to use a finger sleeve?

235
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:08,700
Okay.

236
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Coach,

237
00:17:12,040 --> 00:17:13,500
My string just won't wrap right. It keeps getting stuck.

238
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:14,460
Look.

239
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:18,340
You can't let it get all tangled up.
Right, now try again.

240
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:27,900
Coach, I need to talk to you about something.

241
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:32,700
Just keep an eye on it yourself. I gotta go.

242
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:42,300
Look at Leo, cozying up to the Coach again.

243
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:45,660
His ambition is so obvious!

244
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:50,940
Did Shawn get a clear look?

245
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:52,860
He said he got a clear look.

246
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:55,260
At first, he thought it was just a couple of farmers

247
00:17:55,520 --> 00:17:56,900
spying on us while we practiced our Signature Moves.

248
00:17:57,340 --> 00:18:00,060
But then he saw one of them writing
something down and knew something was off.

249
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:01,540
It turned out

250
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:04,780
It was definitely Jacky and Hugo from Chengnan Team.

251
00:18:12,320 --> 00:18:13,980
Are you absolutely sure he saw clearly?

252
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:15,420
This isn't just a hunch, is it?

253
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,340
You know his eyesight.

254
00:18:18,250 --> 00:18:19,510
I trust him.

255
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:21,660
He wouldn't make up something like this.

256
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:27,900
Maybe we need to

257
00:18:29,120 --> 00:18:31,740
reconsider this whole match.

258
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:35,100
Coach!

259
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:36,540
Someone's here for you.

260
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:38,460
Coach Tony!

261
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:40,860
I've got some news for you

262
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:43,260
that's guaranteed to make your day.

263
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:46,140
As long as you're not here to annoy me.

264
00:18:46,600 --> 00:18:48,060
I'm already more than satisfied.

265
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:51,230
When you put it that way,
it just makes me want to reflect on myself.

266
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:53,820
No, no, that's not what I meant at all.

267
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:56,700
Our School just got another round of funding.

268
00:18:58,120 --> 00:19:01,020
I was thinking, since you guys are always short on funds,

269
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:04,860
why don't we just let our Team cover all the expenses

270
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:08,100
for this Exhibition Match? How about that?

271
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:10,620
See? I didn't come here to make you mad, did I?

272
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:12,830
Oh, I really couldn't accept that.

273
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:14,940
Oh, come on.

274
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:17,340
We're old Classmates. Don't be so polite with me.

275
00:19:18,280 --> 00:19:20,220
Oh, and also...

276
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,590
I wanted to thank you

277
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:24,060
for giving us the morning Training slot

278
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:25,980
on the big platform last time.

279
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:29,430
Oh, it was nothing. Really.

280
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:32,670
Coach Sarah.

281
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:35,100
Jacky and Hugo from your Team,

282
00:19:35,260 --> 00:19:36,540
were they at Practice yesterday?

283
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:37,980
Leo.

284
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:40,860
What do you mean?

285
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:42,270
Coach Sarah.

286
00:19:42,280 --> 00:19:44,220
The whole point of an Exhibition Match
is for Players from both Teams

287
00:19:44,480 --> 00:19:45,770
to showcase their Skills and learn from each other.

288
00:19:46,780 --> 00:19:48,060
But it seems like Chengnan Team wants to win

289
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:50,460
by sneaking a peek at how we practice our Signature Moves.

290
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:54,300
Do you really think a Match like that is still worth having?

291
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:57,190
What? Sneaking a peek?

292
00:19:59,540 --> 00:20:00,540
Do you have any proof?

293
00:20:01,480 --> 00:20:02,940
Sarah, the thing is

294
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:05,820
It hasn't been confirmed yet.

295
00:20:07,520 --> 00:20:09,660
So what you're saying is,

296
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:12,060
it's all just speculation on your part?

297
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:15,900
Tony!

298
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:18,270
I came here in good faith

299
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:19,780
to discuss this Exhibition Match with you.

300
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:21,630
I never imagined

301
00:20:21,640 --> 00:20:23,580
you'd be accusing me of playing tricks behind your back.

302
00:20:24,170 --> 00:20:25,020
Sarah!

303
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:27,900
I have never, ever doubted you.

304
00:20:28,840 --> 00:20:30,300
We're just suspicious of your Players.

305
00:20:30,460 --> 00:20:33,180
Doubting my Players is the exact same thing as doubting me.

306
00:20:34,020 --> 00:20:35,070
My Players spend most of their time

307
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:36,220
Training right alongside me.

308
00:20:37,630 --> 00:20:38,950
I know every single move they make

309
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:40,860
way better than you do.

310
00:20:41,020 --> 00:20:41,820
But we have someone

311
00:20:41,900 --> 00:20:43,260
who saw your Players, plain as day,

312
00:20:43,520 --> 00:20:44,780
sneaking a peek at us practicing our Signature Moves.

313
00:20:44,860 --> 00:20:45,660
Leo!

314
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:48,540
Tony!

315
00:20:49,660 --> 00:20:51,900
I guess all my enthusiasm today was
just one-sided wishful thinking.

316
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:54,780
I guess I never should've come here.

317
00:20:57,640 --> 00:21:00,510
Sarah! Sarah! Wait!

318
00:21:00,520 --> 00:21:01,980
That was just speculation from the Players.

319
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:06,780
It doesn't completely reflect my own opinion.

320
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,180
Then you'd better make your own opinion

321
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:10,920
crystal clear and leave no room for doubt.

322
00:21:11,460 --> 00:21:12,540
So I didn't come all this way for nothing.

323
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:17,340
My opinion, of course,
is that the match goes on as planned.

324
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:22,620
Everything proceeds as usual.

